@page
@model HydroSentinel.Pages.Admin.AdminPageModel
@{ Layout = "_AdminLayout"; ViewData["Title"] = "Help centre"; }
<div class="admin-page-head"><div><p class="admin-page-kicker">Admin handbook</p><h1>Help centre</h1><p>Short guidance for operating the first HydroSentinel admin slice.</p></div><span class="admin-title-pill">Guidance</span></div>
<div class="admin-grid admin-grid-2"><article class="admin-card"><h2>What does demo mode mean?</h2><p style="font-size:12px;color:var(--admin-muted);line-height:1.7">Development demo mode uses the existing server-memory sample store. It does not contact hardware, payment providers, email, or external services. Restarting the app resets the projection.</p><a class="admin-link" asp-page="/Demo">Open demo controls →</a></article><article class="admin-card"><h2>What is available?</h2><p style="font-size:12px;color:var(--admin-muted);line-height:1.7">Navigation, responsive layouts, empty states, PlanCatalog pricing, and read-only projections are ready. Admin identity, audit logs, live telemetry, billing, and support services remain integration work.</p></article></div><article class="admin-card" style="margin-top:18px"><details class="admin-faq" open><summary>Can I use this to control a pump?</summary><p>No. The admin slice contains no hardware commands or control affordances by design.</p></details><details class="admin-faq"><summary>Can I enable demo mode in production?</summary><p>No. The projection checks the host environment and returns an unavailable state outside Development. Query strings and browser state cannot enable it.</p></details><details class="admin-faq"><summary>Where should backend work start?</summary><p>Replace IAdminPortalProjection with authenticated services for customers, devices, telemetry, alerts, billing, support, notifications, and reports while preserving the page contracts.</p></details></article>
